  "description": "Two 150 kg satellites at 550 km, Sun-synchronous. follower-1 starts 2 km behind chief-1 and, on day 1, moves to a passively safe helix around it: 300 m radial and cross-track motion. Impulsive burns, planned with J2 and fired only in sunlight, make the move and hold it. 4 days.\n\nWhat to look at:\n- follower-1.roe_formation.roe: the e and i vectors reach 300 m within 5 hours. a_dlambda first slips to 4 km behind (a burn's partner falls in eclipse), then a drift closes it by day 2.5.\n- follower-1.roe_formation.min_rn_separation: 0 m while behind (the orbits cross), 292 m or more from day 1.2: passively safe.\n- follower-1.roe_formation.delta_v: 0.56 m/s for the move, then 0.026 m/s to hold it to day 4, within 13 m along-track.\n- Explain: the e/i-vector diagram. Events: each burn and drift.\n\nTry changing:\n- Control law Continuous (follower-1's ROE formation): on target by day 1.4, within 3 m from day 2, 1.85 m/s in all.\n- The helix's phase to 0 deg (a_dex = a_dix = 300 m, a_dey = a_diy = 0): J2 turns the inclination vector, and holding costs about three times as much.\n- Generate ROE formation... under the spacecraft list, for another follower.\n\nNote:\n- Near-circular Earth orbits only. The guidance has no differential drag; these satellites are identical.",
  "schema_version": 4
